                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Lieutenant Morris to
                        the captain of the port.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Confederate States Steamer Florida</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Funchal</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1864-02-29"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 29, 1864</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><seg type="margin">[419]</seg> *<hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your letter
                    of the 28th instant, in answer to a communication which you received from me of
                    the same date, setting forth the reasons for my not leaving this port, &amp;c.,
                    has been received. You state that his excellency the governor consents to my
                    being supplied with bread, water, and twenty tons of coals to enable this vessel
                    to proceed to the high seas.</p>
                <p>I will state that I require forty tons of coal to reach the nearest port. I am,
                    sir, with much respect, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C. MARUGAULT MORRIS,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Lieutenant Commanding,
                            C. S. N</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joaquin Pedro de Castelbranco</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Captain of the Port, &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
